  <content>
  <section><title>Warm Up Activity</title>
<para>Which one doesn’t belong?</para>

<div class="os-raise-d-flex os-raise-justify-content-between">
  <para>A.
    <figure><media alt="A line graphed on a set of axes, origin O. Hours versus dollars. The line starts at O and extends up and to the right at a somewhat steep angle."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/ce28f588a2cb1bf8e7630ac1ebb0d8ccb95750be"/></media></figure></para>

  <para>B.
    <figure><media alt="Graph of a line. Vertical axis, hours. Horizontal axis, dollars."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/15f98a6021fbf93233ef7bf2f64a3205285f1c69"/></media></figure></para>
  <para>C.
    <figure><media alt="Graph of 12 plotted points. Vertical axis, dollars. Horizontal axis, hours."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/ac94abdebfe8dfae574d3d13fdb604a25b86bf75"/></media></figure></para>
  <para>D.
    <figure><media alt="Graph of a line. Vertical axis, dollars. Horizontal axis, hours."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/492725157748b37a25d85edb6015c50e4ef6b332"/></media></figure></para>
</div>

<para>Enter your answer here:</para>
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  
  </problem><solution>
    
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  
  <para>Compare your answer: Your answer may vary, but here are some sample responses:</para>
    
    <list>
      <item>A is the only graph that intersects the vertical axis at 0 (or that starts at the origin).</item>
      <item>B is the only graph where the horizontal axis represents dollars and the vertical axis represents hours.</item>
      <item>C is the only graph that is discrete, showing plotted points (that lie along a line) instead of a continuous
        line.</item>
      <item>D is the only graph with a negative slope (or that slants downward from left to right).</item>
    </list>
  
  </solution></exercise></section>
